.TH BC250\-NOSUSPEND 1 "2026-09-07" "bc250-nosuspend 0.1.0" "User Manual"
.SH NAME
bc250\-nosuspend \- persistent block on system suspend
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bc250\-nosuspend
.RI [ COMMAND ]
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bc250\-nosuspend
blocks suspend and hibernation at the systemd level rather than in the settings
of a desktop environment. The block therefore applies equally in KDE, in Gaming
Mode and on a machine with no display attached.
.PP
The block has two parts. First, the targets
.IR sleep.target ,
.IR suspend.target ,
.IR hibernate.target ,
.I hybrid\-sleep.target
and
.I suspend\-then\-hibernate.target
are masked, so every suspend request fails regardless of who made it. Second, a
logind configuration file is created with
.IR IdleAction=ignore ,
so that idling alone does not trigger a suspend.
.PP
Both changes are persistent and survive a reboot.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Shows the state of every systemd target, the
.I IdleAction
value in logind, whether the tool's configuration file is present, and the number
of active inhibitors. Does not require root. Running without any command does the
same.
.TP
.B start
Sets the block. Before making changes it records which targets were already
masked. Running it again on an already blocked system changes nothing.
.TP
.B stop
Removes the block this tool set. Targets that were masked before the block was
set stay masked \(em the tool reports that on standard error.
.TP
.B default
Restores the system defaults: unmasks all five targets regardless of who masked
them, and removes the logind configuration file. An escape hatch for when the
configuration state is uncertain.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Prints the commands that would be executed and exits without making any changes.
Does not require root.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-lang " \fIpl\fR|\fIen\fR"
Message language. Without this option it is taken from the
.B BC250_LANG
variable, then from the system locale; anything unrecognised falls back to
English.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
A short description of the commands and options.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
The version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The
.B status
command returns:
.TP
.B 0
Suspend blocked \(em all targets masked.
.TP
.B 1
Suspend possible \(em no target is masked.
.TP
.B 2
Partially blocked \(em only some targets are masked.
.PP
The remaining commands return 0 on success and 1 on error.
.SH PRIVILEGES
.B status
and any invocation with
.B \-\-dry\-run
run as an ordinary user.
.BR start ", " stop
and
.B default
require root \(em the tool then retries the invocation through
.BR sudo (8).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BC250_LANG
Message language
.RI ( pl
or
.IR en )
when
.B \-\-lang
is not given.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/system/*.target
Masks of the suspend targets, that is symlinks to
.IR /dev/null .
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/logind.conf.d/10-bc250-nosuspend.conf
The
.I IdleAction=ignore
setting for logind.
.TP
.I /var/lib/bc250-nosuspend/previous-mask-state
The list of targets masked before the block was set. On this basis
.B stop
reverses only the tool's own changes.
.SH EXAMPLES
Checking the state:
.PP
.RS
.EX
bc250\-nosuspend status
.EE
.RE
.PP
Previewing the changes without applying them:
.PP
.RS
.EX
bc250\-nosuspend start \-\-dry\-run
.EE
.RE
.PP
Setting the block only when it is not already in place:
.PP
.RS
.EX
bc250\-nosuspend status >/dev/null || bc250\-nosuspend start
.EE
.RE
.PP
Reversing the changes by hand, should the tool be unavailable:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sudo systemctl unmask sleep.target suspend.target hibernate.target \\
                      hybrid\-sleep.target suspend\-then\-hibernate.target
sudo rm \-f /etc/systemd/logind.conf.d/10\-bc250\-nosuspend.conf
sudo systemctl reload systemd\-logind
.EE
.RE
.SH NOTES
The tool does not manage screen blanking \(em that is a separate mechanism of the
desktop environment, unrelated to system suspend. The screen may therefore still
blank while the block is in place.
.PP
For a one\-off block lasting a single command, prefer
.BR systemd\-inhibit (1):
.PP
.RS
.EX
systemd\-inhibit \-\-what=sleep \-\-why="compiling" make \-j16
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd\-inhibit (1),
.BR logind.conf (5),
.BR systemd.special (7),
.BR bc250-mon (1)
.SH BUGS
Report issues at:
.UR https://github.com/zvgelo/bc250-tool-kit/issues
.UE
